      "answer": "The block does not move up the plane.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "*B1: Maximum friction $=0.8(2g\\cos30^\\circ-15\\sin20^\\circ)=9.7521\\ldots$ N.\n*B1: Net force up the plane before friction $=15\\cos20^\\circ-2g\\sin30^\\circ=4.0953\\ldots$ N. If maximum friction is incorrect and $F=ma$ is used, allow for $15\\cos20^\\circ-2g\\sin30^\\circ-\\text{their max }F$.\nDB1: Compare correct values (at least 1 sf): $4.0953\\ldots<9.7521\\ldots$, hence the block does not move up the plane; no incorrect statement.\nAlternative 1: *B1 maximum force down plane $=0.8(2g\\cos30^\\circ-15\\sin20^\\circ)+2g\\sin30^\\circ=19.7521\\ldots$; *B1 force up plane $=15\\cos20^\\circ=14.0953\\ldots$; DB1 compare and conclude no motion.\nAlternative 2: *B1 the scheme prints $F=15\\cos20^\\circ-2g\\sin30^\\circ=4.9053\\ldots$ (printed numerical anomaly retained; the expression evaluates to $4.0953\\ldots$), or $R=2g\\cos30^\\circ-15\\sin20^\\circ=12.1902\\ldots$; *B1 obtain $\\mu=(15\\cos20^\\circ-2g\\sin30^\\circ)/(2g\\cos30^\\circ-15\\sin20^\\circ)=0.3359\\ldots$; DB1 compare $0.3359\\ldots<0.8$ and conclude no motion, with no incorrect statement.\nPrinted total: 3.",
